# Whether an interval x of the round-up interval is in the interior of y (IEEE 1788 interior): x
# empty, or each bound of x strictly inside that of y, or both that bound infinite; the default
# interval_rel_interior_1 on the meanings. Exact, in every rounding mode
# (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Predicates and comparisons"). Requires the rounding mode upward
# set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang
# -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_rel_interior_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
input:         pair stored y = yu yn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
requires:      upward yu yn
ensures:       certain m interior x y x=xu,xn y=yu,yn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the lanes compared, and a test of emptiness (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand

ex = unord(xu, xu)
la = lt(xn, yn)
lb = eq(yn, const inf)
lc = eq(xn, const inf)
ld = and(lb, lc)
lo = or(la, ld)
ua = lt(xu, yu)
ub = eq(xu, const inf)
uc = eq(yu, const inf)
ud = and(ub, uc)
hi = or(ua, ud)
lu = and(lo, hi)
m = or(ex, lu)
